harness: scripts/ladder_vs_cjxl.py --cjxl-flags ours (two cjxl-rs builds
         alternated inside each repeat, leading arm flipped per repeat)
host: Darwin 25.5.0 aarch64 (mac); date 2026-09-10; min of 5
after: current main (all six 2026-09-10 wall fixes)
before: the pre-session build

WHY THIS GRID EXISTS: every other measurement and byte-equality check today used
images <= 2048x2048, which is EXACTLY ONE DC group. Two of the fixes add a
`parallel_map` INSIDE the existing `parallel_map_result(num_dc_groups, ..)`, so
the nested case — more than one DC group — was entirely untested. If rayon
nesting were going to over-subscribe or change results, this is where it would.

Shapes: nature crops at 2560x2560, 3000x3000 and **2500x3100** (deliberately not
a multiple of the 2048 DC-group dimension, so the DC-group grid has partial edge
rows and columns) — each 2x2 DC groups.

BYTES: 9/9 (image, effort) cells byte-identical to the pre-session build, and
18/18 A/B cells byte-identical. Thread determinism separately checked at
t = {1, 2, 8}: no mismatches.

WALL, after/before (<1.00 = faster):

