  median: e3 0.859 (t1) / 0.836 (t8);  e5 0.948 / 0.832;  e7 0.980 / 0.893

No nesting penalty. The t=8 gains are LARGER here (0.83-0.89x) than on the
one-DC-group cells (0.95-0.99x for the same two fixes), which is what more total
parallel work should look like. Note the ratios are against the pre-session
build, so they carry all six fixes, not just the two nested ones.
